## Execution Checklist

> Filled by AI during execution after `deal` is received.
> Check off each item as it is completed.

### Phase 1: Database & Models
- [ ] Create migration file via `make migrate-create NAME=<name>`
- [ ] Apply migration via `make migrate-up`
- [ ] Create/update model in `internal/model/`
- [ ] Update `docs/database.md`

### Phase 2: Data Access Layer
- [ ] Create repository interface + struct in `internal/repository/<domain>/repository.go`
- [ ] Implement all minimal methods (find, find-one, count, create, update, updates, soft-delete, update-or-insert, first-or-create, exists, delete, ids)
- [ ] Register repository in `internal/factory/factory.go`

### Phase 3: Business Logic
- [ ] Create DTO (request/response/filter) in `internal/dto/<domain>/`
- [ ] Create service interface + implementation in `internal/service/<domain>/`
- [ ] Implement all service methods with business rule validations

### Phase 4: HTTP Layer
- [ ] Create handler struct + constructor in `internal/app/<domain>/handler.go`
- [ ] Create route registration in `internal/app/<domain>/route.go`
- [ ] Create one file per action: `create.go`, `find.go`, `find-by-id.go`, `update.go`, `delete.go`
- [ ] Register route group in `internal/delivery/http.go`

### Phase 5: Tests & Verification
- [ ] Write unit tests for service layer
- [ ] Run targeted tests: `go test ./internal/service/<domain>/...`
- [ ] Run full suite: `go test ./...`
- [ ] `go build ./...` passes with no errors
- [ ] Review `git diff` — changes are scoped correctly

### Phase 6: Docs & Commit
- [ ] Update `docs/progress.md`
- [ ] Update `docs/api.md` with new endpoints
- [ ] Commit at logical boundary

